WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
There's a good chance you've either
played flappy bird or at least you've

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.280
heard of it it's easy to play you simply
tap the screen to make the bird fly and

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:11.200
avoid obstacles you get points for
successfully avoiding the pipes but if

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.000
you hit them or crash into the ground
the game is over.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.040
Flappy bird was highly addictive so
much so that it ruined the life of the

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.520
guy who created i. At one point, Dong
Nguyen was making $50,000

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.800
a day on the game from ads yet he
removed it from the App Store and Google

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.520
Play less than a year after its release.
Why did he walk away from what appeared

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.160
to be such a success?
Our story begins in Hanoi, Vietnam in

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.880
2013. Dong Nguyen was a 28-year-old
programmer who lived with his parents. He

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.280
made a living programming location
devices for taxis. As a teen, he was

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.760
obsessed with video games like Super
Mario Bros and also learned to code. He

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.080
played the app Angry Birds but thought
it was too busy, there was too much going

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.960
on. That inspired him to make Flappy Bird
over one weekend. He wanted to make

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.720
something simpler that you could play
while on the go. His company .Gears

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.680
released the game on the App Store on
May 24, 2013. It went live on Google Play

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.080
in early 2014. he decided the game would
be free he hoped to make a few hundred

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.480
bucks a month from the ads within the
game but little did he know the fortune

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.000
that lay ahead.
Initially, Flappy Bird didn't attract

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.240
much attention. Tens of thousands of new
apps come online every month. Competition

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.360
was tough.
However, about eight months after

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.600
releasing the game something strange
happened. People started talking about it.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:37.600
Really talking about it. How they were
addicted to it. How they were frustrated

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.560
by it. How they couldn't stop cursing
after losing.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.360
Flappy Bird adhered to Atari co-founder
Nolan Bushnell's principle: the belief

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.280
that all the best games are easy to
learn and difficult to master.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.600
Whenever you played, you felt like you
could have done better and that made you

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.040
want to try again and again. The game was
all about skill.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.680
Most people usually lost within the
first 10 pipes or so - you got a point for

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.080
every gap you passed through. If you got
10 or more points you did exceptionally

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.280
well.
The physics was especially impressive

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:13.200
Flappy Bird was inspired by the act of
bouncing a ping-pong ball against a

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:17.280
paddle for as long as possible. Whenever
flappy nose-dived, you felt you were

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.000
along for the ride. Whenever flappy died
it wasn't so much that flappy died but

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.680
you died. By January 2014, the game topped
the charts. It was the most downloaded

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.400
app in several countries including the U.S.
It helped that PewDiePie reviewed it

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.920
on his YouTube channel. There we go baby
here we go.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.160
Why is it so hard?
By February 2014, Flappy Bird had been

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.680
downloaded more than 50 million times
netting Nguyen $50,000 a day in ad

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.480
revenue. You'd think he'd be the happiest
man in the world

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.960
but no.
On February 8, 2014 he tweeted that

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.520
Flappy Bird was ruining his simple life
and that he grew to hate his own game.

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:06.160
The following day (local time) he tweeted: 
I am sorry Flappy Bird users. 22 hours from now I

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.440
will take Flappy Bird down. I cannot take
this anymore.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.240
This came as a shock.
Why on earth would anyone remove a game

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.920
that was so insanely popular generating
$50,000 a day even after Apple and

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.400
Google's 30 per cent cut of the revenue?
Instead of being thrilled about his

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.120
success, he was very very unhappy.
In an interview with Rolling Stone a

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.880
month after taking the app offline, he
said he found the sudden intention

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.800
suffocating. He said his parents didn't
know about the game until the paparazzi

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.160
showed up outside his door.
When journalists started reaching out to

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.120
him for interviews he pleaded with them
to "give him peace".

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.720
Even worse than the media attention was
the criticism from some users. He had

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.160
intended for the game to be played for
just a few minutes at a time as a

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.280
relaxing break but in reality, that's not
how people use the app. They were

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.400
addicted.
He showed Rolling Stone a message he

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.240
received from a woman who chastised him
for "distracting the children of the

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:09.040
world." Another person wrote: "13 kids at my
school broke their phones because of

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.280
your game and they still play it because
it's addicting like crack." Nguyen

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:17.120
apparently took these messages to heart:
"...at first I thought they were just

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:22.000
joking but I realize they really hurt
themselves. In an interview with Forbes

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.680
shortly after taking the game down, he
explained it happened to become an

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.240
addictive product: "I think it has become
a problem...to solve that problem it's

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:36.320
best to take down Flappy Bird.
On February 10, 2014 Flappy Bird was no

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.640
more.
Knockoffs soon flooded the app store. It

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.960
was a valiant effort but people still
craved the original. Some tried selling

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:48.160
their smartphones with Flappy Bird
already downloaded for as much as

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.840
$100,000. The game was still
playable there just wouldn't be any

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:56.240
software updates. However, one seller said
eBay canceled his auction because the

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.320
company policy was that the phone had to
be restored to factory settings before

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.680
it could be sold.
After the demise of Flappy Bird, fake

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:08.000
news stories swirled around the creator.
The satirical side Huzlers claimed the

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.240
Flappy Bird creator had committed
suicide. There were suggestions Nintendo

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.240
had threatened to sue him which he
denied the popular gaming site Kotaku

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:20.400
attacked Flappy Bird's creator for
allegedly ripping off Nintendo's art.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:25.280
Kotaku later ended up apologizing.
The addiction, the spotlight, the

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:30.800
criticism all proved too much for Nguyen.
It appears money no matter how much

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:35.920
really can't buy happiness.
Nearly two years after the end of flappy

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.880
bird, Nguyen appeared to be in a much
better place.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.840
In December 2015 he tweeted: "I'm really
happy these days. I finally have a team

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.240
that I fit in and we work together well.
Not alone anymore." He came out with a

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.080
bunch of other games and he said that if
users thought they were too addicting he

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.320
wouldn't hesitate to take them down as
well.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.920
But luckily for him, none would come
close to the success of Flappy Bird.

